  24:../src/Focus_States/Zero_Coarse_State.c **** /**
  25:../src/Focus_States/Zero_Coarse_State.c ****  * @fn State_t Zero_Coarse_State(Context_t*, Event_t*)
  26:../src/Focus_States/Zero_Coarse_State.c ****  * @brief Coarse movement for homing (zero) command
  27:../src/Focus_States/Zero_Coarse_State.c ****  * This uses only the projection of the secondary response onto the primary -
  28:../src/Focus_States/Zero_Coarse_State.c ****  * Re{s/p}  where s = secondary response of lvdt p = primary
  29:../src/Focus_States/Zero_Coarse_State.c ****  * When this value is small enough in magnitude, the state transitions to Zero_Fine_State
  30:../src/Focus_States/Zero_Coarse_State.c ****  * which slows the speed down and continues movement in the same direction until the sign of
  31:../src/Focus_States/Zero_Coarse_State.c ****  * the projection == 0, indicating that the electrical zero of the lvdt has been found. This
  32:../src/Focus_States/Zero_Coarse_State.c ****  * method does not depend on any calibration being present.
  33:../src/Focus_States/Zero_Coarse_State.c ****  *
  34:../src/Focus_States/Zero_Coarse_State.c ****  * @param context State contect for the focus mechanism
  35:../src/Focus_States/Zero_Coarse_State.c ****  * @param event Incoming message (event) in this case, there is no data payload.
  36:../src/Focus_States/Zero_Coarse_State.c ****  * @return The next state for the focus mechanism.
  37:../src/Focus_States/Zero_Coarse_State.c ****  */
